# New UNERA V2 Brand — Output & Standards

Any page, screen, or component built with the **new UNERA V2 brand guidelines** (March 2026 PDF) must follow these rules.

## Output Folder

All new-brand files go in `NewUnera/` (project root). Never edit or overwrite the production root files (`dashboard-enhanced.html`, `wallet-enhanced.html`, etc.) with new brand styles.

```
NewUnera/
  brand-style-guide.html
  dashboard-enhanced.html
  wallet-enhanced.html
  (any future new-brand screens here)
```

## Horizontal wordmark — SVG (canonical)

For **any new or updated** `NewUnera/*.html` page that needs the horizontal UNERA wordmark (nav, dark-side mockups, deep-blue specimens):

- **Full wordmark (e.g. brand guide, full “Unera Stablecoin” lockup):** [`NewUnera/NewLogo/Unera White Text.svg`](NewUnera/NewLogo/Unera White Text.svg) on **dark** surfaces. **`src`:** `NewLogo/Unera White Text.svg` (path relative to the page file).
- **App nav (icon + “Unera” only, no “Stablecoin”):** use [`NewUnera/NewLogo/Unera White Text Nav.svg`](NewUnera/NewLogo/Unera White Text Nav.svg) inside `a.nav-brand`:  
  `<img src="NewLogo/Unera White Text Nav.svg" alt="UNERA" class="nav-logo-img" height="24">`  
  with **`.nav-logo-img`:** `height: 24px; width: auto; max-width: 100%; object-fit: contain; object-position: left center; display: block;` (intrinsic width comes from the nav SVG; no fixed 152px slot).
- **Do not** use `../Brand Guide/Unera-Horizontal.png` for new work; treat the SVGs as the source of truth for V2 pages.
- **Light nav / light surfaces (AA-safe black word):** for the same Unera-only lockup, use [`NewUnera/NewLogo/Unera Black Text Nav.svg`](NewUnera/NewLogo/Unera Black Text Nav.svg). For the **full** horizontal wordmark on light UI, use `NewLogo/Unera Black Text.svg`.

## Typography

Use **TestFoundersGrotesk** via `@font-face` (local OTF files in `Brand Guide/`). Never import Space Grotesk or any Google Font for new-brand pages.

**Canonical Latin files (only these ten — latest brand guideline):** `Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-Light.otf`, `LightItalic.otf`, `Regular.otf`, `RegularItalic.otf`, `Medium.otf`, `MediumItalic.otf`, `Semibold.otf`, `SemiboldItalic.otf`, `Bold.otf`, `BoldItalic.otf`. From `NewUnera/*.html`, reference `../Brand Guide/<filename>`.

```css
@font-face {
    font-family: 'TestFoundersGrotesk';
    src: url('../Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-Regular.otf') format('opentype');
    font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-display: swap;
}
/* Repeat for Light (300), Medium (500), Semibold (600), Bold (700) and matching Italics */
```

Font stack: `--font-display: 'TestFoundersGrotesk', 'Oakes Grotesk', sans-serif;`

**KPI tokens:** `--font-stat-size` (2.5rem) and `--font-stat-size-compact` (2rem) live in `NewUnera/brand-style-guide.html` — use for dashboard-style stat/impact figures.

**Detailed typography (all ten OTF mappings, repo paths, weight 800 anti-pattern, Noto Sans SC, Mada, tabular nums):** `.cursor/rules/newunera-typography.mdc` — align with `NewUnera/brand-style-guide.html` and narrative context in `Brand Guide/Brand Rationale UNERA.docx`.

**P&L and financial direction colors (positive = `--fin-up` / `#1a7a5e`, not `--brand-light-blue`; negative = `--fin-down` / `--brand-red`):** `.cursor/rules/newunera-financial-direction-colors.mdc`.

## No CSS gradients on product HTML

For **any new or updated** `NewUnera/*.html` file **except** [`NewUnera/brand-style-guide.html`](NewUnera/brand-style-guide.html) (which may still show gradient specimens for the PDF brand system):

- Do **not** use `linear-gradient`, `radial-gradient`, `conic-gradient`, or `repeating-linear-gradient` in UI CSS (nav, cards, buttons, titles, icons, bars, overlays, modals).
- Use **`var(--brand-deep-blue)`** for dark brand chrome (nav, primary fills, stepper emphasis) and **`color-mix(in srgb, …)`** with brand tokens for light tints (e.g. 30% yellow / 50% cloud-blue style mixes per the tint swatches in the style guide).
- **`brand-style-guide.html`** is the **only** NewUnera page that should document multi-stop gradients for marketing/specimens.

## Color Tokens (`:root` — use exactly)

```css
:root {
    --brand-deep-blue:   #173d47;
    --brand-yellow:      #ffffab;
    --brand-cloud-blue:  #ebfcf5;
    --brand-earth:       #cec4b8;
    --brand-black:       #000000;
    --brand-white:       #ffffff;
    --brand-red:         #ab5770;
    --brand-purple:      #6a5770;
    --brand-light-blue:  #90c2b8;

    --primary:           var(--brand-deep-blue);
    --accent:            var(--brand-yellow);
    --surface:           var(--brand-white);
    --text-primary:      var(--brand-deep-blue);
    --text-secondary:    #3d6b78;
    --border-subtle:     rgba(23, 61, 71, 0.15);

    /* Product HTML: legacy names hold solids / color-mix only (no CSS gradients). See “No CSS gradients”. */
    --gradient-primary:  var(--brand-deep-blue);
    --gradient-warm:     color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-yellow) 30%, var(--brand-white));
    --gradient-sky:      color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-cloud-blue) 50%, var(--brand-white));

    --success:  #173d47;
    --warning:  #b8a030;
    --error:    var(--brand-red);

    --font-display: 'TestFoundersGrotesk', 'Oakes Grotesk', sans-serif;
    --font-body:    'TestFoundersGrotesk', 'Oakes Grotesk', sans-serif;
}
```

## Key Design Patterns

- **Nav**: Deep Blue background (`#173d47`), white links, Yellow (`#ffffab`) active/hover state
- **Page background**: Cloud Blue (`#ebfcf5`)
- **Primary button**: Deep Blue fill, white text
- **Accent button**: Yellow fill (`#ffffab`), Deep Blue text
- **Cards**: white surface, `border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle)`, `border-radius: 1.25rem`
- **Focus ring**: `outline: 2px solid var(--brand-deep-blue); outline-offset: 2px`
- **Page titles**: solid brand color — `color: var(--brand-deep-blue);` (optionally `font-weight: 700`); do not use background-clip gradient text on product pages

## Icons

All icons across `NewUnera/` use **Material Symbols Outlined** (wght 400, GRAD 0, opsz 24) delivered as **inline SVGs** with `fill="currentColor"`. No emojis, no lucide, no heroicons, no font icons, no SVG sprites. Full specification, markup template, FILL axis policy (outlined vs filled), sizing table, and the canonical 28-icon mapping are in **`.cursor/rules/newunera-icons.mdc`**. The checkmark icon used in steppers and processing trackers is defined in **`.cursor/rules/newunera-checkmark-icon.mdc`**.

## Related rules

- **Custom dropdowns (no native `<select>`):** `.cursor/rules/newunera-dropdown.mdc`
- **Checkbox rows (`.checkbox-label`):** `.cursor/rules/newunera-checkbox.mdc`

## Accessibility (WCAG 2.2 AA)

**Contrast, focus, targets, warm-surface ink, and `--neutral-500` text discipline** for all `NewUnera/*.html`: **`.cursor/rules/newunera-accessibility-wcag.mdc`**.

## What NOT to Do

- ❌ Never use `#10B981`, `#0EA5E9`, or `#EC4899` — those are old brand colors
- ❌ Never import Space Grotesk
- ❌ Never save new-brand files outside `NewUnera/`
- ❌ Never hardcode hex values that have a token equivalent
- ❌ Never use `../Brand Guide/Unera-Horizontal.png` on NewUnera pages — use `NewLogo/Unera White Text.svg` / `Unera Black Text.svg` for the full wordmark, or `NewLogo/Unera White Text Nav.svg` / `Unera Black Text Nav.svg` for app **nav** (Unera-only lockup)
- ❌ Never add CSS gradient functions to product HTML under `NewUnera/` (except `brand-style-guide.html`) — see **No CSS gradients on product HTML** above
